the new year comes several new laws  going into effect and one of them has to  do with gun control and keeping illegal  guns off the street hector mejia joins  us live now from the newsroom hector the  new law bans firearms without serial  numbers tell us more about that that's  correct sherry it is now illegal for a  person to sell and possess firearms that  do not have serial numbers we're talking  about untraceable guns known as ghost  guns this started as assembly bill 286  which was passed last year by state  lawmakers and signed by governor steve  sisilak back in june it targets guns  that can often be made at home from kits  or 3d printers however it has exceptions  it excludes licensed manufacturers guns  made before 1969 antiques or guns that  are permanently inoperable the first  offense is considered a gross  misdemeanor  which is punishable by up to a year in  jail and a potential two thousand dollar  fine after that it becomes a category d  felony if convicted that means time in  state prison between one and four years  that sentence also carries a potential  fine of up to five thousand dollars  supporters of the bill say it's aimed at  preventing gun violence during hearings  we also they also mentioned recent local  shootings particularly the one october  massacre on the las vegas strip and we  also heard from from others the nevada  firearms coalition opposed the bill from  the beginning saying making your own gun  is a hobby for many people reporting  live in our newsroom hector mejia live  local now
 

